//? Title: ShuffleNet: Exact Channel Mixing and Complete Mobile Units
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Grouped pointwise layers save arithmetic but can isolate channel groups. We check both
shuffle orders, expose group connectivity through derivatives, verify v1/v2 unit semantics and
all released budgets, then explicitly fit both complete CIFAR networks with tensor Adam.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.4_efficient_and_mobile_architectures/shufflenet.cpp`.

> The method

For C channels and g groups, the official release moves input channel c to
(c mod g)*(C/g)+floor(c/g). The paper reshapes [g,C/g], transposes and flattens,
which gives the inverse order. These are different permutations when g differs from C/g,
but both can mix the next grouped layer's inputs. The report checks each index, inverse
composition and weighted input derivatives. A shuffle has no learned parameters.

$$\text{two grouped filters:}\quad J=W_2W_1,\qquad
 \text{with shuffle:}\quad J=W_2\Pi W_1.$$
\alttext(A permutation between block-diagonal filters connects groups without adding learned weights.)

With two all-one 12-channel/three-group filters, output zero depends on only the first four
inputs without a shuffle (coefficient four each). Release shuffling connects all twelve inputs:
the first group's coefficient is two, the other groups one. This exact linear fixture exposes
connectivity; it does not prove trained nonlinear blocks use every path or improve accuracy.

V1 reduces with grouped 1×1/BN/ReLU (ungrouped in the very first unit), shuffles, applies
depthwise 3×3/BN, then grouped linear 1×1/BN. Stride one adds x and ReLU; stride two
concatenates a zero-padded 3×3/2 average shortcut with the ReLU branch, producing out-Cin
new channels. Padding counts in the mean: an all-one corner is 4/9. V2 stride one carries
even input channels and transforms odd ones with pointwise/ReLU, depthwise/BN, pointwise/ReLU,
then concatenates carry before branch. This is the release's split/mixing order, without a separate
final paper shuffle. Negative carry values and their exact derivatives survive. V2 stride two
uses the full input in both the projection and learned branch.

Both releases have a 3×3/2 conv/BN/ReLU stem, padded max-pool and 4/8/4-unit stages.
V2 appends a final 1×1 and uses .2 dropout for the 2.0x model only; all classifiers are bias-free
linear maps after global mean. Bias-free He-uniform fan-in initialization is an adaptation;
BN learns scale/shift with epsilon 1e-5. Twelve full 224-pixel width/group budgets below use
measured convolution output shapes. MACs exclude BN, activations, pooling, permutations and
addition and are not measured runtime; the v2 paper warns arithmetic alone does not predict speed.
Complete v1/v2 backward probes retain all widths/sixteen units at 64-pixel synthetic inputs,
shift BN betas and separately check depthwise BN shifts removed by later training normalization.

The two visible fits retain full 1.0x widths and all sixteen units, with v1 groups three and v2
split units. For original 32×32 CIFAR images, small_stem removes only the initial stride/pool;
learned counts are 914328/1265000 and moving counts 24480/16180. Each uses fixed
128 fit/64 validation/64 official-test rows, 6 batch-eight epochs of Adam(.001), explicit
kernel L2=.0001/2 and independent padded crop/flip augmentation. Validation selects paired
learned/moving-state checkpoints before testing. These tiny single-seed runs differ from the
larger original examples and published schedules; they cannot establish an architecture ranking.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/shufflenet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/shufflenet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/shufflenet_concept.tikz > build/shufflenet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/shufflenet_concept.svg build/shufflenet_concept.dvi > build/shufflenet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
